SOAPBOX: this is wq6x's 1st-time running of sac-cw using qrp power.
SOAPBOX: this turned out to be the funnest sac cw gig ever - especially running qrp.
SOAPBOX: it was amazing how often my qrp signal busted thru pileups.
SOAPBOX: i even called cq sac with only one caller.
SOAPBOX: 8-qrp 40-meter qsos to sac is quite an accomplishment from the left coast.
SOAPBOX: find that 20-meters was open to sac from 06:00z to 08:00z was also a treat.
SOAPBOX: the antenna configuration was w 3-el stepp-ir & 2-el shorty-40 - both @55'.
SOAPBOX: look for a write-up on this and other gigs at http://wq6x.blogspot.com
